|MKBHUNGER, BLOOD, AND THE HUNT|000

Feeding establishes one active blood profile: Martial, Predatory, Mystic,
Noble, Vital, or Feral / Profane. Quality ranges from Common through Mythic.
Only living NPC prey and non-player corpses are valid; bloodless creatures,
players, protected prey, and unearned shared-combat targets are rejected.
Careful feeding can leave no evidence when no one notices. Obvious feeding is
seen by nearby living witnesses, and each confirmed witness worsens the local
record. Deep or lethal feeding creates much more Exposure even in private;
feeding on Dawnward's sanctified ground creates especially durable evidence.

|MKBEXPOSURE AND BLOOD MEMORIES|000

Exposure is tracked separately in every area. Its tiers are Quiet (0-9),
Whispers (10-39), Suspected (40-74), and Hunted (75-100). 'bloodsense' shows
the local tier, latest cause, witness count, and known regional totals;
'bloodsense memories' lists significant prey preserved permanently in your
blood. Fallows witnesses can also be asked what rumors name you. Ordinary
evidence fades during quiet time, sanctified evidence fades more slowly, and
coffin rest or a Nameless mask can actively reduce it. Hunted Vampires may be
recognized by Dawnward sentinels or pursued by a blood hunter.

Most significant boss feedings become permanent Blood Memories and grant
Vampire GXP. Four curated bosses also leave a resonance with a permanent
behavioral reward. Lady Vesper strengthens Presence's Awe and changes court
recognition. Lord Blackbriar lets active Obfuscate defeat one witness during
careful feeding. Nhal Serev teaches Bloodsense to identify bloodless prey.
Vaelkor teaches Bloodsense to identify the deep-feed and drain thresholds.
Because Lady Vesper, Lord Blackbriar, and Nhal Serev have no living blood,
meaningful participation in defeating a curated boss can preserve its memory
through the normal class kill-award contract. Use 'bloodsense memories' to
see each known resonance and its exact reward.
Attuned Auspex previews a curated resonance when Bloodsense examines its boss.

|MKBPROGRESSION AND BLOOD MASTERY|000

Vampire GXP survives remort and advances five milestones: The Embrace,
Bloodline Rite, Night Court, Crimson Dominion, and First Night. The final
milestone also requires remort level 750. Knowledge widens as milestones open,
but only three disciplines may normally be attuned; First Night grants a
fourth slot. Attunement changes only at a bound coffin, the First Grave, the
Covenant's Red Chapel, or approved Vespercourt anchors.

GXP and remorts also increase Blood Mastery continuously. Seventy-five percent
of its eventual power comes from an asymptotic GXP curve; the final twenty-five
percent grows across the remort journey through R1000. Blood Mastery improves
bounded discipline damage, healing, duration, and passive combat effects. It
also modestly improves feeding yield, haven recovery, Torpor recovery, and the
Night Familiar. It never raises maximum Vitae or removes Hunger, sunlight,
fire, or holy weaknesses. Use 'vscore' to see the current percentage.

|MKBBLOODLINES|000

At 1,000 GXP choose one permanent bloodline: House Vesper, The Nameless, The
Bloodwrights, The Red Hunt, or The Graveborn. Bloodwrights may vault up to
three active blood profiles, which degrade to Common when recalled.

|MKBDISCIPLINES AND POWERS|000

Each discipline is now a complete mastery track. Foundation powers open when
the discipline is learned; deeper powers require 15%, 35%, 55%, 75%, or 85%
Blood Mastery as listed by 'discipline list'. Celerity, Potence, Fortitude,
Auspex, Obfuscate, Presence, Protean, Animalism, and Blood Sorcery retain their
existing passive and legacy invocations. Dominate opens at Night Court, or at
Bloodline Rite for House Vesper. First Night opens Oblivion. Existing
invocations such as Mend, Mist, Awe, Claws, and the Night Familiar remain
available for compatibility.

Every catalog power declares its Vitae cost, cooldown, discipline, mastery,
target, Hunger behavior, day/night behavior, profile and bloodline mutations,
regional Exposure, boss fallback, and cleanup policy. Ancient encounter powers
share a Vampire major cooldown so several capstones cannot be chained. Bosses
receive bounded damage or debuffs instead of executions or hard control.
Players are never valid targets for Vampire control powers.

Blood profiles mutate matching powers: Martial favors Potence and Fortitude;
Predatory favors Celerity and Animalism; Mystic favors Auspex and Blood
Sorcery; Noble favors Presence, Dominate, and Obfuscate; Vital favors
Fortitude and blood recovery; Feral / Profane favors Protean, Animalism, and
violent Potence at greater frenzy risk. Potent, Exceptional, and Mythic blood
add bounded depth without permanently unlocking abilities.

|MKBPREPARED RITUALS|000

Blood Sorcery can prepare Ward of the Threshold, Sanguine Compass, Seal of
Quiet Earth, Draught of False Life, and Hunter's Malediction. Preparation
costs Vitae and requires an approved Vampire anchor outside combat. The Red
Chapel and Vault of Sealed Earth are Covenant anchors. Prepared uses persist
through logout and remort and are consumed on invocation. Bloodwrights prepare
more efficiently and receive one additional ritual slot.

|MKBWHERE TO BEGIN|000

New Vampires should begin with |GKBvamphelp start|000. Use |GKBvamphelp status|000 to
decode every field shown by vscore. Use 'vamphelp commands' for
the compact topic tree, or ask for a command or power directly, such as
'vamphelp feed' or 'vamphelp quickening'.

|MKBREPAIRING THE COVENANT|000

|YKBVamprepair|000 is a recovery command, not routine maintenance. It preserves
Vampire progression while refreshing the live Covenant soul, autoload,
registered command paths, Vitae registration, runtime hooks, and client
status. It preserves the exact current Vitae amount and never refills it.
Use it after a Vampire update, when class commands are missing, or when an
architect directs you to repair the installation. Active Vampire power
effects end during the refresh.

|MKBOLD RIVALRIES|000

Moonwold werewolves recognize Vampires as ancestral rivals. In their caverns,
each side gains a small offensive edge against the other. Vespercourt instead
recognizes lineage and the Blood Memories carried into court.

|MKBSUNLIGHT, HAVEN, AND TORPOR|000

Open daylight burns Vampires unless the room is inside, underground, or under
canopy. Dawn and twilight are less severe than full day. The class always
retains sunlight, fire, and holy banes. 'discipline mist' provides an emergency
route to the bound coffin when local wards and combat permit it. The Vampire
channel announces dawn, full day, twilight, and night once per transition so
every online Vampire receives the warning even while under cover.

'coffin bind' binds the First Grave, the Covenant's Vault of Sealed Earth, or
Vespercourt crypt as a haven. Resting there restores wounds, steadies low
Vitae toward 75 without lowering a higher pool, and reduces evidence in every
known region. It is recovery, not a full refill or a way around feeding. Once
per reboot, a non-hardcore Vampire death becomes Torpor at the bound coffin.
Torpor begins at one hit point for a new Vampire and recovers up to ten percent
maximum health as Blood Mastery approaches its limit. Later deaths use the
normal death system.

